// SOURCE: examples/voltty/core/main.tach
// The pty (pty.tach): a shell script on a pseudo-terminal through the
// terminal: a 200 KB paste queued and written as the child reads it, a
// colour, the reply to a cursor position report, the exit status.
// ARGS: --run 5 30 --send-n 200000 -- /bin/sh @ROOT@/tests/voltty/paste.sh
// EXPECT: size 5 30
// EXPECT: cursor 4 0 0
// EXPECT: style block 0
// EXPECT: mode 28081
// EXPECT: title -
// EXPECT: tmpl n256 n257 0 - -
// EXPECT: charsets aaaa
// EXPECT: saved 0 0 0 n256 n257 0 - - aaaa
// EXPECT: history 0
// EXPECT: row 0 ready
// EXPECT: row 1 200000
// EXPECT: row 2 red
// EXPECT: attr 2 0-2 n1 n257 2 - -
// EXPECT: row 3 E[3;4R
// EXPECT: row 4 
// EXPECT: end
// EXPECT: exit 0
